+## SMS sign-up
+
+Sign-up verifies a phone number using Twilio Verify before accepting account details. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and supply your Twilio account SID, auth token, and Verify service SID. Configure the service to use 6-digit codes. Without these credentials the form displays an unavailable message and does not simulate verification.
+
+For automatic SMS extraction, enable Twilio Verify's domain-bound OTP setting for the deployed hostname (no protocol or path). Messages must end with `@your-hostname #123456`, using the actual code. WebOTP requires HTTPS and a supported browser; native `autocomplete="one-time-code"`, typing, and pasting remain available. See [Twilio Verify](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api) and [WebOTP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebOTP_API).
+
+The local API stores the pending and approved verification in the server session, enforces a 30-second resend interval and five code attempts, and expires the verification after ten minutes. Account creation forwards the verified phone number to the existing registration service. Configure provider-level rate limits and Fraud Guard in Twilio for SMS abuse protection across sessions.
